.TH "LIST-DIRECTORY-BUCKETS"  "" "" ""
.SH NAME
list-directory-buckets \- 
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
Returns a list of all Amazon S3 directory buckets owned by the authenticated sender of the request. For more information about directory buckets, see \fI\%Directory buckets\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- For directory buckets, you must make requests for this API operation to the Regional endpoint. These endpoints support path\-style requests in the format 
.nf
\(ga\(ga
.fi
\fI\%https://s3express\-control.*region\-code*\fP .amazonaws.com/\fIbucket\-name\fP \(ga\(ga . Virtual\-hosted\-style requests aren\(aqt supported. For more information about endpoints in Availability Zones, see \fI\%Regional and Zonal endpoints for directory buckets in Availability Zones\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP . For more information about endpoints in Local Zones, see \fI\%Concepts for directory buckets in Local Zones\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.IP "System Message: WARNING/2 (<string>:, line 26)"
Inline literal start\-string without end\-string.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Permissions
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
You must have the \fBs3express:ListAllMyDirectoryBuckets\fP permission in an IAM identity\-based policy instead of a bucket policy. Cross\-account access to this API operation isn\(aqt supported. This operation can only be performed by the Amazon Web Services account that owns the resource. For more information about directory bucket policies and permissions, see \fI\%Amazon Web Services Identity and Access Management (IAM) for S3 Express One Zone\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
HTTP Host header syntax
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- The HTTP Host header syntax is \fBs3express\-control.*region* .amazonaws.com\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The \fBBucketRegion\fP response element is not part of the \fBListDirectoryBuckets\fP Response Syntax.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
See also: AWS API Documentation
.sp
\fBlist\-directory\-buckets\fP is a paginated operation. Multiple API calls may be issued in order to retrieve the entire data set of results. You can disable pagination by providing the \fB\-\-no\-paginate\fP argument.
When using \fB\-\-output text\fP and the \fB\-\-query\fP argument on a paginated response, the \fB\-\-query\fP argument must extract data from the results of the following query expressions: \fBBuckets\fP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
  list\-directory\-buckets
[\-\-cli\-input\-json | \-\-cli\-input\-yaml]
[\-\-starting\-token <value>]
[\-\-page\-size <value>]
[\-\-max\-items <value>]
[\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton <value>]
[\-\-debug]
[\-\-endpoint\-url <value>]
[\-\-no\-verify\-ssl]
