.SH OUTPUT
.sp
Buckets \-> (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The list of buckets owned by the requester.
.sp
(structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
In terms of implementation, a Bucket is a resource.
.sp
Name \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The name of the bucket.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
CreationDate \-> (timestamp)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Date the bucket was created. This date can change when making changes to your bucket, such as editing its bucket policy.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
BucketRegion \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBBucketRegion\fP indicates the Amazon Web Services region where the bucket is located. If the request contains at least one valid parameter, it is included in the response.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
BucketArn \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the S3 bucket. ARNs uniquely identify Amazon Web Services resources across all of Amazon Web Services.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This parameter is only supported for S3 directory buckets. For more information, see \fI\%Using tags with directory buckets\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
